    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67165">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_61775"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Physical anatomical entity which has mass. Examples: hemoglobin molecule, mitochondrion, hepatocyte, erythrocyte, heart, head, blood, urine.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fma</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">From UBERON:

Anatomical entity that has mass.

http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon.owl</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Material anatomical entity</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67292 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67292">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_61817"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fma#regional_part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_62000"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The right cerebral hemisphere is one of two bilateral, largely symmetrical organ subdivisions within the telencephalon which contain the cerebral cortex and cerebral white matter.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fma</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">From UBERON:

A cerebral hemisphere that is in the right side of a brain.

Equivalent to http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon.owl</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Right cerebral hemisphere</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67325 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67325">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_61823"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fma#regional_part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_61817"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Occipital lobe is the one of five lobes of the cerebral hemisphere which occupies the posterior-most portion of the hemisphere.  Anteriorly, it shares an arbitrary border with the parietal lobe and temporal lobe.  Medially, it is bounded by the longitudinal cerebral fissure.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Occipital cortex</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Occipital region</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fma</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:label>Occipital lobe</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67329 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67329">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_61823"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/fma#regional_part_of"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_61817"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The insula is the one of five lobes of the cerebral hemisphere. It lies in the depths of  the lateral fissure and is covered by portions of the frontal, parietal and temporal lobes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Central lobe</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Cortex of island</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Insula lobule</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Insular cortex</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Insular lobe</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Insular region</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Island of Reil</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fma</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:label>Insula</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67504 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67504">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FMA_67135"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Anatomical structure, which is a subdivision of a cardinal body part; it may exclude bones; is demarcated from other subdivisions of the same cardinal body part by anatomical surfaces or lines or topographical references; together with other contiguous subdivisions of the same cardinal body part, it constitutes a cardinal body part. Examples: thorax, perineum, back of neck, forearm, hand, phalanx, nose, auricle of ear, scrotum.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Principal body part subdivision</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>fma</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <rdfs:label>Subdivision of cardinal body part</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


