    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010106 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010106">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010107"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A neuropsychological testing battery administered as part of the ADNI1 project that is used to establish a baseline assessment of study participants&apos; level of cognitive functioning.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Alexander P. Cox</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>ADNI baseline visit cognitive testing assay</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>ADNI baseline visit neuropsych battery assay</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>Alzheimers disease neuroimaging initiative baseline visit neuropsych battery assay</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>From the ADNI1 procedures manual revised:

&quot;The goal of ADNI neuropsychological testing is to use standardized procedures to objectively and reliably assess a subject’s cognitive abilities.&quot;</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Alzheimers disease neuroimaging initiative baseline visit cognitive testing assay</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010107 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010107">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010002"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010002"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cognitive functioning assay that is composed of multiple cognitive functioning assays.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Alexander P. Cox</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>neuropsych battery</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>neuropsych test battery</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>neuropsych testing battery</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <obo:IAO_0000118>neuropsychological test battery</obo:IAO_0000118>
        <rdfs:comment>&quot;Neuropsychological tests measure and quantify specific parameters of mental functions, such as short and long term memories, different causes for speech language and learning impairments, and impaired motor, visual and spatial functions, among others. The results often provide valuable information about the location of the disorder in the brain.&quot;

From: http://www.cognitivetestingservices.com/test-neuropsychological-battery.php</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>neuropsychological testing battery</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010108 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010108">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010002"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0020149"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0020150"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0020151"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0020152"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0020153"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000299"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0020154"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000114 rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000123"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The ADNI boston naming assay invloves promting subjects with pictures of items and recording if the subject correctly names them. Both semantic and phonemic cues are given if the subject is unable to respond. Six outputs are calculated by the tester: the total correct without a cue, the total correct with a semantic cue, the total correct with a phonemic cue, the total sematic cues given, the total phonemic cues given, and the total of all of all correct responses with or wothout a cue (0-30 inclusive). Total phonemic and semantic cues are not used in the final score, and are for clinical use only.

&quot;This reduced version of the Boston Naming Test is a measure of the ability to orally label (name) 30 line drawings of objects. The objects are presented in order of frequency, from most frequent (i.e., bed) to least frequent (i.e., abacus). This test is sensitive to aphasia and also to object recognition deficits. For the purposes of the ADNI, only the odd-numbered items from the full test will be administered.&quot;</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>This assay has five specified outputs:

1. Number of spontaneously given correct responses
2. Number of semantic cues given
3. Number of correct responses following a semantic cue
4. Number of phonemic cues given
5. Number of correct responses following a phonemic cue
6. Total Number Correct (1+3)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Mark Jensen</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <obo:IAO_0000119>http://www.adni-info.org/Scientists/ProceduresManuals.aspx#</obo:IAO_0000119>
        <rdfs:label>ADNI boston naming test assay</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011000 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011000">
