        <obo:IAO_0000115>An assay objective to measure one or more cognitive functions of the evaluant.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Alexander P. Cox</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:label>cognitive function measurement objective</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011003 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011003">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000963"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A categorical label that indicates the level of cognitive functioning that the categorical measurment datum represents.

*** REVISIT ***</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Alexander P. Cox</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>*** NOTE ***
It is currently asserted that the subclasses of &apos;cognitive functioning categorical label&apos; denote their respective level of cognitive functioning; however, this is not wholly appropriate since the &apos;denotes&apos; relation is defined as an &quot;instance level relation&quot; and it is used here between classes.  This is a hang-over from switching these label entities from individuals to classes and will need to be addressed at a later point in development once the individual-class usage has been ironed out in NPT.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>cognitive functioning categorical label</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011004 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011004">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011001"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000312"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0010000"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A cognitive functioning measurement datum that is the specified output of the realization of a Folstein mini mental examination.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Alexander P. Cox</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>*** QUESTION ***
Is this the specified output of a Folstein MMSE or is the proper specified output the numerical measurement datum and this categorical measurement datum is a secondary output (or the specified output of another assay that has the numerical measurement datum as its specified input and has this categorical measurement datum as its specified output)???</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Folstein mini mental state examination cognitive functioning categorical measurement datum</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


