    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011015 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NPT_0011015">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000104"/>
        <metadata:prefixIRI>NPT:0011015</metadata:prefixIRI>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A plan specification comprised of protocols (which may specify how and what kinds of data will be gathered) that are executed as part of an investigation and is realized during an assay.

-IMPROVED TO-

A plan specification that is concretized in an assay plan and is comprised of protocols that specify how and what kinds of data will be gathered.

*** REVIEW ***</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000117>Alexander P. Cox</obo:IAO_0000117>
        <rdfs:comment>*** NOTE ***
This class and its definition are modeled on the class &apos;study design&apos;.  As such, both classes currently commit the following mistake: a plan specification is an information content entity and not a realizable entity.  Thus, while an assay design or study design can be concretized in a plan and that plan can then be realized, it is not accurate to state that an assay design can be realized by/during/etc. an assay.  This confusion is caused by OBI&apos;s attempt to bypass the need to deal with &apos;plan&apos; and should be reexamined before NPT is released.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>assay design</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


